[h1]v1.9.0[/h1]

[h2]New[/h2]

[list]
  [*]Added the [b]Incinerate[/b] ammo mod for the Powerstave, which turns it into a flamethrower.
  [*]Added _Challenge Scaling_, which allows players to reduce their Project 45 weapons' damage should they feel that they're too powerful. This feature decreases Project 45 weapons' final damage by the percent set in the settings.

[list]
  [*]Added the [b]Challenger's Will[/b] mod, which incentivizes increasing the Challenge Scaling by rewarding currency per kill (or after dealing 450 health damage)
[/list]
  [*]Added the [b]Auto-9[/b], based on Robocop's Auto-9 pistol.
  [*]Added distinct chamber indicator sprites for ballistic, energy and experimental weapons. Some weapons are also given their own chamber indicators.
  [*]Added the [b]Pyroclast[/b], a weapon that deals substantial fire damage but explodes and jams when you overcharge it.
  [*]Added the [b]Bullet Cutter[/b], a barrel mod for ballistic weapons that increases multishot. Incompatible with ballistic shotguns and other certain ballistic weapons.
  [*]Added the [b]Project 45 catalog[/b]; can be bought in the Project 45 Gun Shop
  [*]Added distinct projectile sprites for the bladed, explosive, elec and poison arrows.
  [*]Added dedicated labels for charge and trigger time on the gun tooltip.
  [*]Added mods that modify the gun's cocking and reload time
  [*]Added the **Shrapnel** and **Reaper**, a lever-action and revolver based on the Zweibrandyr.
  [*]Added the [b]Phasma[/b], a plasma pistol.
  [*]Added the [b]Smart Pistol[/b] from Titanfall.
  [*]Added the [b]Electric Zi[/b], which can be obtained by applying the transformer kit of the same name onto Machine Pistols 

[list]
  [*]The Electric Zi (Transformation Kit) is craftable at the Gunsmith Addon, under the new "TRNS" section
  [*]Transformer mods act as Portable GDKs; the guns are disassembled when applied, and opening the disassembled weapon returns the installed mods and the new weapon.
  [*]Transformation can be disassembled; doing so returns the transformer mod.
  [*]Transformation kits are consumed upon use.
[/list]
  [*]Added the [b]SMG-K[/b], a compact, more customizable version of the SMG.
  [*]Added the [b]Flared Magwell[/b], a mod that slightly decreases reload cost and time.
  [*]Added the [b]Developer's G.D.K.[/b], a reusable Portable G.D.K. Craftable at the Replicator with the Gunsmith Addon.
  [*]dyeing works now but needs a custom script and items that use that script.
  [*]Added new dyes to the shops under the "Util" section.
  [*]The Solarium Alloy mod can now change a weapon's color (if the weapon is properly configured)
  [*]Added the [b]Fan Hammer[/b], a stock mod for revolvers that turns them full-auto.
  [*]Added the [b]Flashlight[/b], which is basically like the Laser Beam but flashlight.
  [*]Added the [b]Saint H.A.L.O[/b], a simple energy pistol.
  [*]Added dedicated gun shops for each weapon category. ('project45-ballisticgunshop', 'project45-energygunshop', 'project45-experimentalgunship')
  [*]Added [b]Subsonic Rounds[/b], which doubles damage but makes ballistic weapons manual-feed.
[/list]

[h2]Changes[/h2]

[list]
  [*]Changed tracer rendering method for almost all projectiles. Instead of spawning a streak particle of static length, projectiles now use a script that draw a streak particle from their previous position to their current position.
  [*]Changed sprite used by almost all bullets, arrows and other projectiles into an animated one; The above change causes projectiles fired by other entities to not have streaks, so the sprites were improved to look good even without the streaks.
  [*]Firetime is now divided into its constituents: charge time, cycle/cock time and trigger time. This should make it clear how fast guns can dole out damage.
  [*]Increased recoil reduction of the Violium Alloy Parts from default to 3.
  [*]Added an indicator for Awakened Weapons
  [*]Added tooltip information on what to do once you've applied Essential Gun Oil onto a gun. (Replaces the gun's flavor text)
  [*]Changed rarity of Portable G.D.K from essential to common.
  [*]Changed name of Neo-Compound Bow to 'Neo-Penobscot Bow'.
  [*]Improved Electric Ammo VFX
  [*]Improved Energy Weapon SFX
  [*]Demoted Magma Spitter into an SSR experimental weapon, and changed its item ID. Old Magma Spitters are marked with a red '(!)'; it is recommended you replace them with the changed Magma Spitter.
  [*]Improved the Project 45 Manual codex.
  [*]Halved price of the Supply Transponder (Gacha puller) and both kinds of Cipher Keys (Gacha tickets).
  [*]Added Cipher Keys to the drop tables
  [*]Removed stray crafting recipe from the Gunsmith Addon
  [*]Decreased sell factor of the Reimburser from 1x to 0.8x.
  [*]Added increased selling prices for particular items sold via the Reimburser:

[list]
  [*]reagents
  [*]Unique Project 45 Items
[/list]
  [*]Balanced the effects of Ammo Consume Chance; If a gun fails to consume ammo, then it will consume exactly 1 energy or 1 stocked ammo.
  [*]Changed bullet impact SFX
  [*]Add bullet impact sfx to hitscans, chain hitscans, beams, chain beams, and summoned projectiles.
  [*]Reworked item drops so that they drop in the form of cases and unknown stat mods, instead of themselves, so that gathering them won't result in a cluttered inventory. XSSR stat mods still drop as themselves.
  [*]Decreased the weight of the max level mod.
  [*]Increased the weight of the SSR Wildcard mod.
  [*]Made stat drops more consistent:

[list]
  [*]for planet difficulties 0-1, there is a 6% chance to drop a tier 1 unknown stat mod, and a 4% chance to either drop a level mod or a Beginner's Crutch.
  [*]for planet difficulties 2-3, there is a 3% chance to drop a tier 2 (diff. 2) unknown stat mod and a 1% chance to drop a level mod.
  [*]for planet difficulties 4-5, there is a 1% chance to drop a tier 3 unknown stat mod, or a level mod.
  [*]for planet difficulty 6, there is a 0.5% chance to drop either ONE tier 3 unknown stat mod or a level mod.
  [*]for planet difficulty 7 and beyond, there is a 0.5% chance to drop either ONE tier 3 unknown stat mod or a XSSR mod (i.e. either a god mod or an admin mod).
[/list]
  [*]moved level mod drop to respective unknown stat mod drop tables
  [*]fixed bad item weights in drop tables.
  [*]The Kinetic Arbiter and Gauss Rifle no longer ignore terrain when shooting at full charge.
  [*]Improved Project 45 Configuration UI to be more informative.
  [*]The projectile conversion mod now changes the weapon's projectile based on its category; ballistics will fire bullets, energy and experimentals fire lasers.
  [*]Added VFX to reload and jam bars, affected by the Performance Mode setting.
  [*]The Essential Gun Oil now causes any dye applied onto the weapon to be conserved and not consumed.
  [*]Changed how recoil is applied onto the current weapon offset.
  [*]Changed the rarity and price of the Orbital Transponder from Legendary (SR) to Essential (XSSR).
  [*]Expanded the categories present in the Gunsmith's crafting Menu.
  [*]Added rarity colors to gun and mod tooltips.
  [*]Increased padding of stat numbers in the mod tooltips.
  [*]Changed how certain guns spawn magazine particles on reload.
[/list]

[h1]Balancing[/h1]

[list]
  [*]The following projectiles have been given arming distances of 10 blocks:

[list]
  [*]The default projectiles of the Hand Mortar, Grenade Launcher and Rocket Launcher
  [*]Thermite Grenades
  [*]Cluster Grenades
[/list]
  [*]Added a random speed modifier (mean = 1, st. dev = 0.1) to projectiles fired from guns, improving how they look.
  [*]decreased project45splitblade projectile speed from 150 to 100
  [*]increased project45splitblade time to live from 0.05s to 0.1s
  [*]decreased project45splitbladefragment speed from 150 to 90
  [*]Nerfed the ability to get rich easily with Project 45 items.

[list]
  [*]Decreased price of almost all project 45 items to 10% of their original value.
  [*]Items sold in the Project 45 gun shop now have a 10x inflated price point.
[/list]
  [*]cock time and mid-cock delay stat modifications are now separated from fire time stat modification, and joined into reload time stat modification
  [*]changed fire time stat mod numbers so that the approximate breakpoint at which multiplicative mods are more beneficial than additive mods is at 500ms (cycle/cock time).
  [*]changed how fire time stat mods are applied; instead of divvying up the additive cycle time modifier, the modifier is directly added to all aspects of the gun's firing time (cycleTime, chargeTime and overchargeTime, and fireTime a.k.a. trigger time)
  [*]Reduced the damage multiplier provided per weapon level.
  [*]Changed how supercrits are calculated:
```
alpha = 0.4
Scaling = BCD / (1 + alpha * (BCD - 1))
FCD = BCD + ln(T) * Scaling
```
where FCD is the Final Crit Damage, BCD is the Base Crit Damage and T is the crit Tier.

This way, a Tier 1 crit is still consistently the BCD, and higher tiers increase the FCD with diminishing returns. The higher the BCD is, the harsher the diminishing; the damage increase from a T1 crit to a T2 crit is higher than the damage increase from a T7 crit to a T8 crit, and the damage increase from a T2 crit to a T3 crit is higher on a gun with 2x BCD than a gun with 4x BCD.

Before this formula, a weapon with 300% CC and 5x CD can deal a minimum of 7x damage. Now, it deals ~6.6x damage.

[list]
  [*]Decreased reload Rating Multiplicative Damage for Good and Perfect Reloads from 1.25 to 1.125 and 1.5 to 1.25, respectively.
[/list]
  [*]Fixed how the damage multipler from stocking ammo is calculated.
  [*]Changed how Melee Swipe damage is calculated.

[list]
  [*]Buffed the damage factors of the Bayonet Grip's swipes.
  [*]Nerfed the Underbarrel Chainsaw by removing its recoil stats and decreasing its per-tick damage from 0.5x to 0.3x.
[/list]
  [*]Nerfed the recoil recovery time and delay of Malorian Arms 3516. The low firerate of the gun allowed it to recover completely before the player can shoot again, ensuring consistent accurate fire, so I gave it a bit of recoil.
  [*]Nerfed the God Mod by increasing its upgrade cost from 3 to 5 and decreasing its stack limit from 3 to 2.
[/list]

[h2]Fixes[/h2]

[list]
  [*]Removed the ability to install mods on weapons with a non-matching category.
  [*]Fixed script crash when upgrading weapons on a Weapon Upgrade Anvil.
  [*]Fixed Enemy Flares spawning enemies in ship worlds
  [*]Disabled lowercase-global warnings in apply.lua
  [*]Fixed crash caused by disassembling guns.
  [*]Refactored NPC main behavior script so that it calls the old init() function instead of completely overwriting it
  [*]Fixed script crashing issues with Fleetly Fading's alt ability.
  [*]Fixed bug with manual reload alt ability
  [*]Improved how buildproject45mod.lua changes the string of the slot shown in the mod's tooltip.
[/list]

<!-- Motivation: I attempted to make a subsonic ammo mod that turns semi/auto guns manual-feed. Despite showing that I have indeed made an "ammo" mod, the presence of augment.gun makes my code classify it as a mod belonging to the "unknown" slot unless I specify the slot it belongs to. If I do specify the slot, the slot shows up in the tooltip as "ammoType", which looks ugly. This change will allow me and other modders to be explicit with the slot under the hood. -->

[list]
  [*]Added stat mod tooltip colors to crit damage
  [*]Updated description of The Admin Mod
  [*]Fix possible cause of script crashes
  [*]Made fixes to Reimburser UI
  [*]Fixed upgradeable guns still appearing in the upgrade anvil UI even after upgrading it.
  [*]Fixed the Stasis status effect preventing entities from dying until the effect expires.
[/list]

